    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our premier option. With an elite efficiency score of 81.88, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Scherzer\u2019s 5.10 xERA, bolstered by a 19% SP skill advantage and a \"slow delivery\" factor that drastically increases the probability of a stolen base\u2014a critical multiplier for our scoring strategy. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** also registers as a strong start (72.65), as he similarly exploits the soft matchup against Bassitt. Despite neutral platoon splits, **Kyle Tucker** (66.32) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (63.76) remain locked in our daily rotation, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically seeing a 14% boost due to dynamic platoon data against McLean.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **Wade Meckler**, who finished just shy of our \"Strong\" threshold with a score of 38.82. While his park factors and batting order position were advantageous, the negative variance provided by Cavalli\u2019s efficiency led the optimizer to prioritize our current starters to conserve game caps. Meanwhile, **Liam Hicks** (36.92) was bypassed primarily due to a difficult matchup against an elite pitcher (2.27 xERA), which punished his raw projection beyond the point of viability. \n\nWe are monitoring two \"Lineup Pending\" statuses: **Kyle Tucker** and **Jackson Merrill**. **Jackson Merrill** carries a solid 59.98 score, aided by favorable wind conditions and a strong platoon split, but his efficiency is slightly tempered by a 1.0% penalty for an elite defensive catcher. As we navigate the final stretch of the season, maintaining our edge in stolen bases remains the priority; we will keep **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci** on high alert should late-game pinch-running opportunities arise to capitalize on the weak pitching staff facing our lineup tonight.",
